# Opt-in only: Qt 6.8.3 library-internal Memcheck records (reviewed exception).
# See DEVELOPMENT-WORKFLOW.md, "Memcheck exceptions". Not a GC memory fix.
#
# Every stanza was generated with --gen-suppressions=all from the pure-Qt control
# program in qt-6.8.3-webengine-control/ (no GoldenCheetah code), offscreen and on
# xcb in the UI gate's environment, with the runners' Memcheck flags, and kept only
# if it matches a gate or fixture record offline or Valgrind used it in a gate or
# fixture run with the candidate files. A stanza is the control's chain up to the
# first program frame ("program") or to a thread root ("complete"), or a cut inside
# the libraries: where the stack enters another Qt library ("library"), after
# QEventDispatcherGlib::processEvents ("dispatcher") or at --num-callers
# ("truncated"). Cuts inside the libraries need at least 7 library frames and a
# named frame on the path, match only leaks (never error records), and, if all
# frames are unnamed objects, only indirect ones. Names: <n>-<kind>-<cut>-<named|objonly>.
# Library objects are written as obj:*/<soname>*; the exact builds are pinned in
# qt-6.8.3-webengine.supp.buildids and the runners refuse this file if a pinned
# library's Build-ID differs. A stanza ending at QEventDispatcherGlib::processEvents
# leaves out only the program's event-loop driver above it.
#
# Keep the unsuppressed report of every run. Regenerate from the controls and
# re-verify after changing Qt, libc, any pinned library or Valgrind.

